---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import FlowDiagram from '../components/FlowDiagram.astro';
import { REPO_URL, REPO_API, DOCS_URL } from '../consts';
import symbolLight from '../../brand/favicons/symbol-color_1024.png';
import symbolDark from '../../brand/favicons/symbol-dark_1024.png';

const quickstart = [
  'git clone https://github.com/metricminellc/metricmine.git && cd metricmine',
  'uv sync',
  'make demo-fetch',
  `uv run python -c "from metricmine.query import GoldWarehouse; print(GoldWarehouse().list_fact_categories())"`,
].join('\n');
---

<Base>
  <!-- hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Contract-driven data pipeline</p>
        <h1 class="display">Agents propose.<br />Humans approve.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          MetricMine is an open source data pipeline that ends in an answer,
          not a table. AI drafts the data contracts. A person approves every
          change before deterministic code builds the warehouse. Every step is
          versioned, reviewed, and auditable.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={REPO_URL}>View on GitHub</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={DOCS_URL}>Read the docs</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
        <img
          class="symbol-light"
          src={symbolLight.src}
          width="1024"
          height="1024"
          alt=""
          loading="eager"
        />
        <img
          class="symbol-dark"
          src={symbolDark.src}
          width="1024"
          height="1024"
          alt=""
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- the flow -->
  <section class="flow-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">The flow</p>
        <h2>From raw data to a governed answer.</h2>
        <p>
          Machines do the repeatable work. People keep the judgment. Nothing
          reaches the warehouse without an approval on record.
        </p>
      </div>
      <FlowDiagram />
      <p class="mono-note">
        Agents propose. Code executes. A human approves. The full architecture
        and its committed evidence live in{' '}
        <a href={REPO_URL}>the repository</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- why -->
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Why it works this way</p>
        <h2>Built on three rules.</h2>
        <p>
          Most data contracts are documentation. MetricMine makes them the
          enforced interface between a pipeline and the AI agents that use it.
          Contracts generate models. Models generate contracts. Both are
          gated. A human approves every change.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        <article class="card">
          <svg
            class="cube"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 18 18"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <polygon points="9,1 16,5 9,9 2,5" fill="#B4DACC"></polygon>
            <polygon points="2,5 9,9 9,17 2,13" fill="#5CAC94"></polygon>
            <polygon points="16,5 16,13 9,17 9,9" fill="#25444C"></polygon>
          </svg>
          <h3>Contracts before code.</h3>
          <p>
            Every dataset is shaped by a contract a person approved. Change the
            contract and the change is visible, versioned, and reversible.
            Under the hood: ODCS 3.1.0, enforced at build time and tested in
            CI.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <svg
            class="cube"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 18 18"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <polygon points="9,1 16,5 9,9 2,5" fill="#B4DACC"></polygon>
            <polygon points="2,5 9,9 9,17 2,13" fill="#5CAC94"></polygon>
            <polygon points="16,5 16,13 9,17 9,9" fill="#25444C"></polygon>
          </svg>
          <h3>Humans hold the gate.</h3>
          <p>
            AI proposes and explains. It never merges its own work. A person
            approves every contract and every generated model before anything
            runs. Under the hood: two proposer agents, pull requests, an
            ownership manifest.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <svg
            class="cube"
            width="20"
            height="20"
            viewBox="0 0 18 18"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <polygon points="9,1 16,5 9,9 2,5" fill="#B4DACC"></polygon>
            <polygon points="2,5 9,9 9,17 2,13" fill="#5CAC94"></polygon>
            <polygon points="16,5 16,13 9,17 9,9" fill="#25444C"></polygon>
          </svg>
          <h3>Deterministic and local.</h3>
          <p>
            The pipeline runs end to end on one laptop. Same inputs, same
            outputs, every time. Built small by design: the patterns are the
            same ones that run at enterprise scale on any cloud. Under the
            hood: dbt Core and DuckDB.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- for engineers -->
  <section class="eng-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">For engineers</p>
        <h2>Run it locally.</h2>
        <p>No cloud account, no cluster, no signup. Python 3.12 and uv.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="quickstart">
        <pre><code>{quickstart}</code></pre>
        <button id="copy-btn" class="copy-btn" type="button">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-row">
        <a class="chip" href={REPO_URL} id="star-chip">
          <svg
            width="14"
            height="14"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="currentColor"
            aria-hidden="true"
          >
            <path
              d="M12 2l2.9 6.26 6.86.6-5.2 4.55 1.55 6.72L12 16.57l-6.11 3.56 1.55-6.72-5.2-4.55 6.86-.6z"
            ></path>
          </svg>
          <span id="star-text">Star it on GitHub</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script define:vars={{ REPO_API, quickstart }}>
    // Copy the quickstart block.
    const btn = document.getElementById('copy-btn');
    btn?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(quickstart);
        btn.textContent = 'Copied';
        setTimeout(() => (btn.textContent = 'Copy'), 1600);
      } catch (e) {
        btn.textContent = 'Select and copy';
      }
    });

    // Live star count, verifiable social proof only. Fails silent.
    fetch(REPO_API)
      .then((r) => (r.ok ? r.json() : null))
      .then((data) => {
        const n = data && data.stargazers_count;
        if (typeof n === 'number') {
          document.getElementById('star-text').textContent =
            `${n} ${n === 1 ? 'star' : 'stars'} on GitHub`;
        }
      })
      .catch(() => {});
  </script>

  <style>
    .hero {
      background: var(--mm-hero-wash);
      padding-block: 88px;
    }

    .hero-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: center;
      gap: 48px;
    }

    .hero-art {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .hero-art img {
      width: min(280px, 60vw);
      height: auto;
    }

    .symbol-dark {
      display: none;
    }

    :global([data-theme='dark']) .symbol-dark {
      display: block;
    }

    :global([data-theme='dark']) .symbol-light {
      display: none;
    }

    @media (max-width: 820px) {
      .hero {
        padding-block: 64px;
      }

      .hero-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .hero-art {
        order: -1;
      }

      .hero-art img {
        width: min(160px, 40vw);
      }
    }

    .flow-band {
      background: var(--mm-bg-raised);
      border-block: 1px solid var(--mm-border);
    }

    .cards {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 22px;
      margin-top: 12px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 820px) {
      .cards {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }

    .card {
      background: var(--mm-card-bg);
      border: 1px solid var(--mm-border);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .card .cube {
      margin-bottom: 14px;
    }

    .card h3 {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }

    .card p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--mm-text-2);
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
    }

    .eng-band {
      background: var(--mm-bg-raised);
      border-top: 1px solid var(--mm-border);
    }

    .quickstart {
      position: relative;
      margin-top: 8px;
    }

    .quickstart pre {
      background: var(--mm-code-bg);
      border: 1px solid var(--mm-border);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 20px 110px 20px 20px;
      overflow-x: auto;
      margin: 0;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .quickstart code {
      color: var(--mm-text);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }

    .copy-btn {
      position: absolute;
      top: 12px;
      right: 12px;
      font-family: var(--font-manrope);
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 0.8125rem;
      color: var(--mm-btn-text);
      background: var(--mm-btn-bg);
      border: none;
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 7px 12px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .copy-btn:hover {
      filter: brightness(1.08);
    }

    .proof-row {
      margin-top: 22px;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
